WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.550
A puck slides across a frictionless
surface in a dead straight line.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.230
It never turns and never curves.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.440
A fixed post stands just off its path.

4
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.100
A spinning wheel has angular momentum.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.920
So does a satellite on a circular orbit.

6
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.970
But this puck is not
going around anything.

7
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.060
Does it carry any angular
momentum, measured about the post?

8
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:27.200
In this mission, you'll send a child
running onto a still merry-go-round,

9
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.670
and work out how fast it turns.

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.830
Then you'll follow a satellite
around a stretched orbit,

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.380
and compare its speed near
the planet and far away.

12
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.880
Your mission: decide whether the
straight-moving puck has angular momentum,

13
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.550
measured about the post, and explain why.
